    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> of the House of Savoy that united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italy">Italy</a> between 1859 and 1870 and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> its capital in 1871.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>, appointed in 1922, it became the first Fascist dictatorship and built a colonial empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a>.</li><li>Defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#second-world-war">Second World War</a> discredited the monarchy, and a referendum in 1946 replaced it with a republic.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Italian troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> in 1870 through a breach in the walls at Porta Pia, and the popes then lived as self-declared prisoners in the Vatican until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lateran-treaty">Lateran Treaty</a> of 1929.</p></aside>
    </section>

